{
  "_comment": "Governance contracts read on Ethereum mainnet, one entry per governance system. `source` is the protocol's own address registry the addresses were taken from; every address was checked on-chain on 2026-10-18 (the method answered as the kind expects). `contracts` lists what is read, in order: the first contract that reports a delay gives the headline, so the executor's timelock comes first. Kinds: timelock (Compound-style `delay()` / Sky DSPause), oz-timelock (`getMinDelay()`), aave-payloads-controller, lido-timelock, lido-dual-governance, governor (GovernorBravo / OZ Governor parameters; `token` names the unit), aragon-voting, safe (`getThreshold()` / `getOwners()`), holder (`method` returns a privileged address, which is then described as EOA, Safe or contract), rocket-dao-security.",
